From 01b14638d1699bbc93b3a08283e3010d9a25e50f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domingo Alvarez Duarte <mingo@Domingos-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:43:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(generate): report every unresolved conflict, not
 just the first

`handle_conflict` returned the first conflict it found as an error, so a
grammar with n independent conflicts took n `generate` runs to triage, one
pair per run, with no way to see what was still hiding behind the first
one. A grammar ported from bison hits this immediately: its conflicts come
from the port, not from the original grammar, so there are usually several
at once.

Collect them instead. A conflict that the grammar does not declare is
recorded, the state keeps both actions as if the conflict had been
declared, and state building continues; the tables are discarded either
way, and carrying on is what reaches the states behind the one that
conflicted. Conflicts are deduplicated by symbol set, so a pair is
reported once however many states run into it.

The report for a single conflict is unchanged: the item sets and the
precedence that would resolve it are what an author needs. With several,
the message summarizes: one line per conflict, with the `conflicts` entry
it needs. `--json-summary` still returns the full item sets.

For the PostgreSQL 16 grammar, this turned 12 sequential runs into one
0.4 s run that lists all 12 conflicts.
